class.description:
Add states as children of a [BehaviorStateMachine], one node a state, named for what the agent is doing ("Patrol", "Chase"). Write what a state does in a script extending it:
[codeblock]
extends BehaviorState

func _enter():
    agent.play("run")

func _update(delta):
    var target: Node3D = blackboard.get("target")
    if target == null:
        transition_to("Search")
        return
    agent.chase(target, delta)
[/codeblock]
[member agent] and [member blackboard] are the outermost machine's: its parent, and its dictionary of shared values.
